# Anchor Program Standards

## Structure
- One program per directory under `programs/` (e.g., `programs/escrow/`, `programs/payout/`)
- Separate `state/` module for account structs, `instructions/` for handlers
- Use `#[account]` with explicit `space` calculation — never hardcode sizes

## Security Checklist
- Validate all signers and account ownership before state mutation
- Use PDAs with deterministic seeds: `[b"escrow", policy_id.as_ref()]`
- Check account discriminator on deserialization
- No `unwrap()` in production code — use `?` with custom `ErrorCode` variants
- Implement circuit breaker: pause flag on escrow account, settable by authority

## Escrow Pattern
```rust
// ✅ GOOD — explicit space, authority check, PDA seeds
#[account(
    init,
    payer = authority,
    space = 8 + EscrowAccount::INIT_SPACE,
    seeds = [b"escrow", policy_id.as_ref()],
    bump
)]
pub escrow: Account<'info, EscrowAccount>,
```

## Error Handling
- Define errors in `error.rs` using `#[error_code]`
- Map oracle failures to distinct error codes (e.g., `OracleStale`, `OracleLowConfidence`)

## Dependencies
- Use `anchor-lang` and `anchor-spl` — do not add unvetted crates
- Pyth SDK: `pyth-sdk-solana` for on-chain price reads
